 "final_text": "The theorem in `/work/putnam_2007_b5.lean` is now proved. `lean /work/putnam_2007_b5.lean` compiles with no errors and no `sorry` warning. The only output is a linter style suggestion about `<;>` in the `hG1` proof, which I left as is.\n\n**Approach:** Let `m = \u230an/k\u230b`, so `n - k\u00b7m` is an integer in `[0, k)`. Define the monic polynomial `G(T) = \u220f_{j<k} (T \u2212 (n \u2212 j)/k)` with coefficients in `\u211d[X]`, where `X` stands for `n`. Then `m` is a root of `G` at `n`, because `(n \u2212 j)/k = m` for `j = n \u2212 k\u00b7m`. Divide `T^k` by `G` with `modByMonic`, giving `T^k = q\u00b7G + R` with `deg R < k`. Evaluating at `(n, m)` kills the `q\u00b7G` term. The coefficients `P_i = R.coeff i` then give the required identity.",
